# XSH tcgetwinsize()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# Terminal tests use a pseudo-terminal (XSI), for which the page promises a default size
# and the values last set. Only ws_row and ws_col are compared: the page does not
# define other members.

assertion  XSH.tcgetwinsize.001
anchor     functions/tcgetwinsize.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/tcgetwinsize.html#RETURN VALUE
class      conditional
when       BASE|XSI
since      2024
says       tcgetwinsize() on a pseudo-terminal subsidiary whose size was never
           set returns 0 (the default size is unspecified and is not compared).
note       XSI only for the pseudo-terminal set-up (posix_openpt() and its
           companions are XSI); the requirement itself is Base. A set-up that is
           not available is UNRESOLVED, or NOTINUSE when the facility is absent.
test       t/001-default.c

assertion  XSH.tcgetwinsize.002
anchor     functions/tcgetwinsize.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/tcgetwinsize.html#RETURN VALUE
class      conditional
when       BASE|XSI
since      2024
says       After tcsetwinsize() with 31 rows and 97 columns, and again with 7
           rows and 200 columns, tcgetwinsize() returns 0 and exactly those
           values.
note       XSI only for the pseudo-terminal set-up (posix_openpt() and its
           companions are XSI); the requirement itself is Base. A set-up that is
           not available is UNRESOLVED, or NOTINUSE when the facility is absent.
test       t/002-after-set.c

assertion  XSH.tcgetwinsize.003
anchor     functions/tcgetwinsize.html#ERRORS/EBADF
class      required
since      2024
says       tcgetwinsize(-1) and tcgetwinsize() of a closed descriptor return -1
           with EBADF.
test       t/003-ebadf.c

assertion  XSH.tcgetwinsize.004
anchor     functions/tcgetwinsize.html#ERRORS/ENOTTY
class      required
since      2024
says       tcgetwinsize() of descriptors for a regular file, both ends of a pipe
           and /dev/null returns -1 with ENOTTY.
test       t/004-enotty-file.c

assertion  XSH.tcgetwinsize.005
anchor     functions/tcgetwinsize.html#DESCRIPTION
class      conditional
when       BASE|XSI
since      2024
says       A size set through one descriptor of a pseudo-terminal subsidiary is
           returned by tcgetwinsize() on a second descriptor after the first one
           is closed.
note       XSI only for the pseudo-terminal set-up (posix_openpt() and its
           companions are XSI); the requirement itself is Base. A set-up that is
           not available is UNRESOLVED, or NOTINUSE when the facility is absent.
test       t/005-persist.c
